Z||000000||yaya842m4||12-23-2001||09:33 AM||||i have an 84 2m4,turned the car off the other day and then it would not start(the stater would not even engauge).i figured it was a bad started solenoid.so i bought a new one but before installing i thought i try to start the car just in case,and it started on the first try,so what i'm asking,could the solenoid be faulty,or could this be a heat problem in the engine compartment...any ideas or solutions would be most welcome<P>------------------<BR>||||reg||11
Z||000001||California Kid||12-23-2001||09:48 AM||||Could just be the ignition switch, or switch that determines if trans is in park or neutral. If it happens again, make sure you're turning the key fully forward with a little force.||||reg||1
Z||000002||GTDude||12-23-2001||08:19 PM||||One more thing......make sure your battery cable connections are clean.  Very important!<P>Phil Pettus<P>------------------<BR>GTDude's 86GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||85 gt fiero||12-23-2001||08:30 PM||||im not sure what they call it but if the starter gets hot it wont start for a while even if its -100*F out its something to do with a solenoid i think.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Posthumane||12-23-2001||10:49 PM||||I had this problem with my 84 SE. Basically when the starter solenoid gets old, it tends to not work when hot. If you let it cool down enuf, it will eventually go. Putting a heat shield around it is a temporary fix, but eventually you will have to replace the solenoid anyway. Since you already have one, that's no prob. Also, make sure the cables going to the starter aren't touching the exhaust in any way.||||reg||1
